<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    Combined-payload validation manifest for the disposition LOI stage-narrowing wave
    (agent-output/disposition-loi-stages.md, items A1-A6, A9). Lists every constructive
    declarative component this admin pass touched, so it can be check-only validated in the
    SAME transaction as manifest/loi-disposition-stage-narrow/destructiveChangesPost.xml -
    exactly the ordering the design doc's §5.2 requires (A6's flexipage edit removing the two
    LOI__c.Mark_Countered_By_DPEG / LOI__c.Mark_Counter_Received <valueListItems> references
    MUST land before, or in the same transaction as, their QuickAction deletion in A7/A8, or
    the delete fails with "This action is referenced elsewhere in Salesforce").

    This is a validation-only convenience manifest. The REAL deploy for this wave uses
    --source-dir force-app (the full constructive payload, including the Apex/LWC half the
    developer agent owns) per the design doc's §5.2 atomicity requirement, not this narrow
    list - do not use this file as the real deploy's --manifest.
    -->
